zlib for OpenVMS
================

This is zlib @VERSION@ built natively for OpenVMS @ARCH@, from the
unmodified zlib release plus the patches in the vms-zlib project:

    https://github.com/issinoho/vms-zlib

Kit version: @KITVERSION@.  zlib is distributed under the zlib licence;
see LICENSE.  The API is described in ZLIB.TXT (from the zlib.3 manual
page) and in ZLIB.H itself.

What is installed
-----------------
    ZLIB$ROOT:[INCLUDE]ZLIB.H, ZCONF.H   the zlib API
    ZLIB$ROOT:[LIB]LIBZ.OLB              the library (object library)
    ZLIB$ROOT:[BIN]MINIGZIP.EXE          zlib's small gzip program

Setting up
----------
The kit installs ZLIB$STARTUP.COM into SYS$STARTUP and runs it once.  To
define ZLIB$ROOT at every boot, the system manager adds this line to
SYS$MANAGER:SYSTARTUP_VMS.COM:

    $ @SYS$STARTUP:ZLIB$STARTUP.COM

Building a program against zlib
--------------------------------
    $ CC /INCLUDE=ZLIB$ROOT:[INCLUDE] myprog.c
    $ LINK myprog, ZLIB$ROOT:[LIB]LIBZ.OLB/LIBRARY

The library is compiled with /NAMES=AS_IS; zlib's names are all shorter
than 31 characters, so /NAMES=(AS_IS,SHORTENED) works as well.

minigzip
--------
    $ minigzip :== $ZLIB$ROOT:[BIN]MINIGZIP.EXE
    $ minigzip "-9" file.txt          ! -> file.txt-gz
    $ minigzip "-d" file.txt-gz

minigzip reads and writes raw bytes, so a VFC or variable-record file
keeps its record structure in the compressed data; use it on Stream_LF
files for exact Unix-compatible results.
